  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implements exact QQ Mumford serialization, Cassels--Flynn/Mueller Kummer coordinates, direct sparse Flynn quartic duplication, cached certified canonical heights, pairings and regulators. Primitive integral classical quintics use an exact model-specific duplication L1 audit, Stoll root-partition bounds, certified archimedean correction partial sums/tails, and the factorization-free modular-gcd finite correction of Mueller--Stoll Section 14. Public and private proof records, cached Kummer points, ball matrices, diagnostics, and provenance are immutable or defensive-copy safe; strict replay covers supplied torsion certificates, integral basis transforms, regulator index scaling, and rigor state. Caller-supplied bounds remain explicitly conditional and cannot drive a local decomposition. Exact-coordinate limits count rational model denominators and enforce both conservative pre-duplication and exact post-duplication checks. Tests cover cache poisoning, resource limits, torsion zero, scaling, basis transforms, the full h2!=0 generalized Kummer transform, seeded constructed-divisor differential corpora against Cantor, nontrivial finite gcd content, and genuine Magma V2.18 CanonicalHeight/HeightPairing/regulator values.",
    "risks": [
      "Automatic certification and local-correction decomposition require a primitive integral odd quintic with h=0; generalized h remains exact direct Kummer arithmetic but numerical unless a proved caller bound is supplied.",
      "Even-degree transformations, number fields, and genus 3 are deliberately outside this lane.",
      "The finite engine implements the certified factorization-free modular approximation to arbitrary precision, not the optional exact coprime-factor formal logarithm representation.",
      "The archimedean engine is a certified bounded-exact, projectively normalized iterator. Exact coordinate size still grows by roughly fourfold in bits per step; a default 100000-bit guard prevents runaway work, so this is not an arbitrary-precision optimized phase exit.",
      "architecture:check reaches package-graph validation but the new claimed modules exceed the existing hyperelliptic-curves-algorithms lazy byte budget; integration must split or raise that centrally owned manifest budget."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Wire canonical_height, height_pairing, regulator, and capability methods into the centrally owned public Jacobian API and package graph.",
      "Add both strict modules to the central pyright configuration and run integration-owned Linux, Windows, macOS, and Wasm suites.",
      "If exact formal finite corrections are useful to researchers, add the optional Bernstein coprime-factor refinement atop the existing modular gcd sequence."
    ]
  }
